id: pmc-itemless-pending
title: Preserve itemless Dependabot release notes across tagging
description: "Dependabot-only default notes for pending itemless windows, retained in tagged itemless windows only when their immutable changelog contains the exact version heading. Preserve historical projection otherwise. PR #311; pm-context recovery plan remains unexecuted."
type: Issue
pm_format_version: 2
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-changelog#311"
created_at: "2026-11-02T04:43:41.380Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-02T11:45:56.911Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-02T11:45:55.268Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-02T11:45:55.268Z"
author: codex-sol
resolution: "Itemless windows render Dependabot-only notes (--no-merges) when pending, or when the tag's committed changelog already has the version heading; every other historical window stays byte-identical. The CLI resolves --output against the process cwd before reading the tag's changelog."
expected_result: "Dependency-only releases get truthful Dependabot notes that survive tagging, with zero churn in committed history."
actual_result: "release:check 1001/1001 with 100% lines, branches and functions; 12 revert mutations fail as required; zero churn in pm-beads, pm-jira, pm-slack and pm-starter; pm-context gains its pending 2026.11.1 notes by design (recovery plan on this item)."
comments[21]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-02T04:43:44.199Z",codex-sol,"Scope and links: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli-companion/blob/main/.agents/pm/issues/pm-cli-website-tbni.toon and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli-companion/blob/main/.agents/pm/issues/pm-cli-website-mcrq.toon. Preserve historical output and existing release thresholds; add real-git regression and revert checks; open PR and wait for CI, then record recovery plan only."
  "2026-11-02T04:46:32.306Z",codex-sol,"Current origin/main already rejects missing requested sections with MissingRequestedReleaseError/MISSING_REQUESTED_RELEASE before output. Reuse that canonical selector and guard. Automatic git notes apply only to itemless pending tag windows; explicit true preserves Dependabot enrichment for history, explicit false disables notes. Plain version-only tracker generation does not infer a git range. Generic git subjects remain escaped literal text."
  "2026-11-02T04:50:36.691Z",codex-sol,"Focused source and extension verification: node --test test/itemless-pending.test.ts test/extension.test.ts passed 28 tests, zero skipped. Real-git cases cover Dependabot-only, generic workflow-pin-only, no commits, pending items plus commits, byte-identical historical windows, single-window cutoffs, pending --stdout --limit 1, and opt-out. Revert proof is wired into the existing lifecycle CI job."
  "2026-11-02T04:56:14.648Z",codex-sol,"Final focused verification passed 8/8 tests after adding recorded-hash fallback for an empty git subject. pm test --run --only-last --progress passed the source-only disposable revert proof: fixed 8 pass, fallback revert 4 fail, restored 8 pass; requested-release guard fixed 1 pass, guard removal 1 fail, restored 1 pass. Full release gate is still running at unchanged thresholds. No consumer repository edits are needed for the new default."
  "2026-11-02T04:58:27.219Z",codex-sol,"Opened https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/311 at 23fba9866b450673771242dbf929d72aea920e7a. PR links this item and its history plus companion pm-cli-website-tbni and pm-cli-website-mcrq. CI lifecycle and CodeQL queued; Semgrep running. Build, test typecheck and docstring gate passed: 39 files and 264 documented declarations. Wait for green CI before inspecting and recording pm-context recovery."
  "2026-11-02T05:24:30.349Z",codex-sol,"CI at 23fba9866b450673771242dbf929d72aea920e7a: lifecycle passed (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/41391251311/job/125102917149), CodeQL/codeql and Semgrep passed. Lifecycle log confirms our generator proof fixed/restored 8 pass and default revert 4 fail; CLI guard fixed/restored 1 pass and removal 1 fail. Node 22 and Node 26 jobs are running full npm and Bun gates. Sourcery skipped, Cubic neutral, Greptile trial ended: these provide no review approval."
  "2026-11-02T05:28:52.390Z",codex-sol,"The local pm-linked npm run release:check attempt reached its 2400-second timeout while existing native lifecycle and Unicode suites were active; assertion_failure=0, timeout=1. It is incomplete evidence. Increased only this new item's linked command timeout to 7200 seconds and rerun the identical release gate; package thresholds and commands are unchanged. CI lifecycle, CodeQL and Semgrep passed; Node 22/26 full gates are still running."
  "2026-11-02T05:43:03.069Z",codex-sol,"Diagnosed the preflight failures as stale local dependencies, not a feature regression or a demonstrated sandbox defect: installed pm-cli 2026.10.20, pm-ops 2026.10.19 and marked 18.1.1 disagreed with the lockfile. npm ci installed exact pm-cli 2026.10.27, pm-ops 2026.10.26 and marked 18.1.2; lockfile unchanged. The same isolated existing host/SDK test now passes directly and through the pinned pm runner on Node 26.13.0. Interrupted the invalid-install rerun; it is not passing evidence. Restart the unchanged full gate on the corrected install. CI npm gates on both Node 22 and Node 26 have passed; Bun gates are running."
  "2026-11-02T05:53:59.252Z",codex-sol,"Actual Git-base revert proof, in a disposable archive: git archive ff74b2c97752ec6d12c11de51d95f9fee0c4608c src package.json; copy the new regression file and shared git fixture, link the exact installed dependencies, run node --test test/itemless-pending.test.ts. Base: 8 tests, 3 pass, 5 fail, zero skips. Restore current src in the archive: 8 pass, zero fail/skips. Existing no-commit, item-bearing and history controls pass on the base; default rendering, single pending fallback, opt-out/help and empty-subject checks detect the full revert. CI Node 26 completed both npm and Bun release gates: 985/985 tests each, 0 skips, 28 measured source files with 100% lines/branches/functions; docstrings 264 declarations across 39 files; production audit 0 vulnerabilities. Job: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/41391251311/job/125110075165. Statements are not independently measured by this package's gate."
  "2026-11-02T06:01:50.032Z",codex-sol,"Initial code head 23fba9866b450673771242dbf929d72aea920e7a is green: lifecycle, test (22), test (26), CodeQL/codeql and Semgrep succeeded. Both Node jobs completed npm and Bun full gates with 985 tests, 985 pass, 0 fail/skips, 28 source files and 100% lines/branches/functions on every pass. Node 22 job https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/41391251311/job/125110075105; Node 26 job https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/41391251311/job/125110075165. Begin read-only pm-context recovery investigation now; no workflow dispatch, merge or release authorized."
  "2026-11-02T06:19:46.909Z",codex-sol,"Recovery plan and evidence recorded in this item's body after green CI. Verified the exact existing resume shell block in a disposable clone, including two-bullet extraction and refusal controls. A plain notes-only repair fails the pinned canonical check; the verified two-commit notes/receipt lineage keeps canonical CI unchanged and supplies a preserved main-ancestor recovery_notes_sha. All actual pm-context state remains unchanged. Future execution needs separate authorization."
  "2026-11-02T06:33:46.106Z",codex-sol,"Corrected-install local npm run release:check passed through the pinned pm runner on Node 26.13.0: 985/985 tests, 0 fail/skips; LCOV lines 8715/8715, branches 3156/3156, functions 566/566 across all 28 required source files; docstrings 264/264 declarations in 39 files; production audit 0 vulnerabilities; package/changelog/date/publish-attestation checks passed. Actual host argv proof also passed for both pm changelog generate and export: default exit 0 with git Dependencies, --no-dependency-updates exit 1 for the missing requested section. Earlier stale-install timeout/interrupted runs are not passing evidence; the corrected full run and green Node 22/26 npm/Bun CI replace them. The recovery plan remains unexecuted; item stays in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-02T07:53:59.691Z",codex-sol,"Review follow-up: remove generic commit notes and preserve itemless Dependabot sections across tagging only when the changelog committed at that tag already contains the exact version heading. Add real CLI squash/merge transition regressions, committed-path and no-history-churn probes, exact revert counts, and five disposable origin/main consumer checks. Keep the existing pm-context recovery plan unexecuted; its prepared changelog has no matching heading. Run the unchanged release gate with a 7200-second timeout, commit tracker evidence with code, and push only this PR branch."
  "2026-11-02T08:02:12.954Z",codex-sol,"Implemented Dependabot-only non-merge collection and immutable tag-blob heading retention, with changelogPath documented for SDK and forwarded from CLI/extension output. Focused real-git regressions pass 22/22 with zero skips; extension generate/export custom-output transition passes 1/1. The first merge-fixture run exposed an unfixed synthetic merge date; pinning fixture dates made both fleet transitions pass. Full release gate is active through the pinned pm runner at timeout_seconds=7200. The first disposable consumer attempt hit only a bin permission issue after replacing dist; preserve npm executable permissions in the swap and rerun. No consumer remote writes or recovery actions."
  "2026-11-02T08:09:17.551Z",codex-sol,"Independent exact review-head revert evidence: archive src/package/manifest from aa4d1541c461be251f8f4826131bd56624de83ad into a disposable copy, add the current regression file, run node --test against it: 22 tests, 11 pass, 11 fail, zero skips. Restore current source: 22 pass, zero fail/skips. The required consumer measurements exposed an existing preflight interaction: pm-beads real origin/main fdf4dfcf91222819ab9c839c59d672ee9a172681 with tag v2026.11.01 has no matching committed heading, and the new build correctly omits it but full-file --check is refused by the existing MISSING_REQUESTED_RELEASE guard. Measuring pinned-generator baselines and all five consumers before changing guard scope. pm-context remains untagged; its required pending default may intentionally add a section, so an unconditional five-repo zero-churn expectation needs clarification. No consumer state was pushed or changed."
  "2026-11-02T08:19:29.333Z",codex-sol,"Resolved the tagged-only compatibility issue within the requested rule: unbounded full-file all-tag generation/checks preserve canonical sectionless history; stdout and limited/since-version requests still require their requested section. Added real CLI pending/tagged full-file checks and matching extension checks, with strict extraction controls and behavioral reverts. Restarted the full 7200-second release gate on this source after stopping the earlier run; that stopped run is incomplete evidence. Fixed the revert harness to recognize the expected typed extension refusal rather than requiring every behavioral mutant to throw an AssertionError. pm-context baseline is up to date at 2f226a219b91184e8e0e8f68cce68bfe6c52bf63; the new build adds its required pending Dependabot section, so that live five-repo zero-churn requirement conflicts with rule (a). The pending clarification does not change its recovery plan or authorize execution."
  "2026-11-02T08:42:04.348Z",codex-sol,"Final disposable origin/main measurement through pm test --run --only-index 4 --progress: all five pinned-generator baselines report up to date. Frozen CLI/generator fingerprint c7af8174854021f277f1d9ec3808a5d93ebbf361b24c85ed219dd7de7c16b4c9; fetched all remote tags, including orphaned tags, before each repository-own npm run changelog:full -- --check. Candidate results: pm-beads fdf4dfcf91222819ab9c839c59d672ee9a172681 PASS/up to date, changelog SHA256 182bd5cdb2a3c3ae3d9d4de8d9fefb30ea0e9cbb6812c853a3432093cfce27f8; pm-jira c041906ab4e4ca41d8a5e35b1b8f278c20456490 PASS/up to date, a499ff101f031b4988840f635c03362d0b888a69686a7f03d005241b5e50d9d4; pm-context 2f226a219b91184e8e0e8f68cce68bfe6c52bf63 FAIL/out of date, adds heading 2026.11.1 - 2026-11-01 for its untagged Dependabot-only pending window; pm-slack 7df7ac4307a96dde300f98dd553dc80620865126 PASS/up to date, 54fddc02242eee99c1e30cedb46bef2f4f8ad5842c6d61107fe90b6c5d481330; pm-starter 499affe0ebec21a8a16d8ebb35b975d4022d8265 PASS/up to date, 9ca244e8d31c13123ef1af9e0893dfc9d5af50fd49814e2840dd735c5d5e8c6f. All working changelog files remained byte-identical under --check; no consumer remote writes. The five-consumer assertion correctly fails 4 != 5. Its unmet pm-context criterion conflicts with mandatory pending rule (a), not tagged-history retention. Preserve the specified rendering rule pending clarification; do not claim five-repo zero churn or execute recovery."
  "2026-11-02T08:42:06.359Z",codex-sol,"Final revert proof passed through pm test --run --only-index 2 --progress, timeout_seconds=1800. Eleven independent disposable mutations have exact fixed/reverted/restored counts: default-disabled 3/3/3; tag-retention-removed 8/8/8; history-rewritten 5/5/5; generic-subjects-restored 1/1/1; merges-restored 1/1/1; empty-subject-hash-restored 1/1/1; generate-output-path-removed 1/1/1; export-output-path-removed 1/1/1; full-history-refusal-restored 2/2/2; extension-full-history-refusal-restored 1/1/1; requested-release-guard-removed 1/1/1. Middle counts are failing tests; fixed/restored counts are passing tests, all with zero skips. Exact aa4d154 review-head archive with 24 standalone tests: 11 pass/13 fail; restored source: 24 pass/0 fail/skips. Expanded extension regression passes 1/1. SDK exact-version/path checks pass 3/3, preserving case in 1.0.0-RC.1 headings. README/help and dist are rebuilt. Full release gate remains active at unchanged thresholds and timeout_seconds=7200."
  "2026-11-02T08:54:13.963Z",codex-sol,"After the transient provider interruption, rechecked branch and tracker: source changes are intact, claim remains codex-sol and item stays in_progress. The pm wrapper was interrupted, but its detached exact npm run release:check child survived and its complete captured stdout/stderr remain available. Continued monitoring that already-running gate rather than restarting completed checks. Revert proof and all five consumer results were already saved and were not rerun. No source or threshold changed after the final gate began."
  "2026-11-02T09:24:43.278Z",codex-sol,"Final unchanged npm run release:check completed successfully on Node 24.19.0. The original pm test wrapper was lost during the provider interruption; the surviving exact npm child completed every &&-chained stage with intact captured stdout/stderr, ending with the successful publish-attestation receipt. No completed checks were restarted after recovery. Tests: 1001/1001 across 49 suites; fail/cancel/skip/todo all zero; test duration 3277912.948683 ms. LCOV: lines 8734/8734, branches 3170/3170, functions 568/568 across all 28 required source files, unchanged 100% thresholds. Docstrings: 265 declarations across 40 files. Production audit: 0 vulnerabilities. Package allowlist and content scan: 107 files each, 0 failures. Canonical changelog/link check, release date and publish attestation all passed. Final CLI/generator fingerprint matches the five-consumer build c7af8174854021f277f1d9ec3808a5d93ebbf361b24c85ed219dd7de7c16b4c9. The separate five-consumer criterion remains explicitly unmet at 4/5 because required pending rule (a) adds pm-context 2026.11.1 notes. Preserve its recovery plan without execution. Commit code, dist and tracker receipts together, push only this PR branch, leave item in_progress and release the claim. No CI wait, thread replies, mentions, merge or release."
  "2026-11-02T09:39:42.423Z",claude-orchestrator,"Orchestrator review of 37ec0b6: the stable-tagging rule is correct (itemless window keeps Dependabot-only, non-merge notes when pending or when the changelog committed at its tag has the version heading). One defect fixed by the orchestrator: the CLI passed --output unresolved while the generator resolves relative paths against gitCwd, so with --pm-cwd naming another directory the tagged section was lost (reproduced: MISSING_REQUESTED_RELEASE). Now passes resolve(options.output), matching the extension. New regression test 'CLI resolves --output from the process cwd even when --pm-cwd names another directory' plus mutation cli-output-path-unresolved in the revert proof: all 12 mutations fail on revert and pass restored. pm-context's added pending 2026.11.1 section is the correct rule-(a) behaviour for its stuck untagged release, not history churn; the other four repos are zero churn."
